ence.","H5":"This outcome was not registered, so these tests are post hoc. Detection of AI-generated posts was higher under the AI Accuracy Nudge by 6.6 points (95% CI [1.4, 11.9], p=0.014), the Breathing Exercise by 9.1 points (95% CI [3.2, 15.0], p=0.003) and the AI Literacy Guide by 7.9 points (95% CI [0.0, 15.7], p=0.049). The other eight arms were not distinguishable from control.","H6":"This outcome was not registered, so these tests are post hoc. Recognition of authentic posts was lower under AI Literacy Infographic 2 by 6.1 points (95% CI [−11.1, −1.0], p=0.019). The other ten arms were not distinguishable from control, with intervals spanning zero. Taken with H5, this hints that some arms shift how people classify posts rather than raising accuracy overall.","H1a":"Excluding respondents with low political knowledge (a knowledge screen, not an attention check) cut the sample to about 70%. Automated Flagging stayed at +3.6 points (95% CI [0.1, 7.2], p=0.044), smaller. The AI Literacy Guide fell to +2.3 points (95% CI [−3.0, 7.7]) and Mindfulness to −3.7 points (95% CI [−8.3, 1.0]). Intervals widened, so the effects shrank and became noisier; the registered conclusions are unchanged.","H2a":"Without covariates, Breathing Exercise remained lower on attitudes toward AI, by 0.63 points (95% CI [−1.12, −0.15], p=0.011), close to the adjusted −0.54. Other arms remained within about 0.3 points of control with intervals spanning zero. The Breathing Exercise result does not depend on covariate adjustment, so the registered conclusion holds."},"exploratory":{"E1":"This unreviewed check reports that excluding 613 respondents made the two accuracy effects non-significant, but its table has empty estimate columns, so nothing displayed supports the claim. The reviewed robustness rerun (H1a) is the better guide.","E2":"This unreviewed check reports no arm reaching p<0.05 within low or high AI-familiarity subsamples, but its table shows no estimates, so the claim cannot be verified from what is displayed.","E3":"This unreviewed placebo check found no intervention related to pre-treatment knowledge (all p ≥ 0.116), which is consistent with successful randomisation."},"limitations":"Eleven arms across four registered outcomes yield 44 tests with no multiplicity correction, so several nominal results near p=0.05 may be chance. Some arms have under 100 respondents, giving wide intervals. Some data were collected before registration. Outcomes are measured in a single online session with a panel sample, so durability and real-world feeds are untested. The exploratory outcomes (H5, H6) are post hoc, and the pipeline's own exploratory checks are unreviewed. Non-significant arms are inconclusive rather than evidence of no effect."}
